{
  "claim": "For non-headline series with an available offer panel and no active 14-day stability gate, analog forecasts will reduce pinball loss relative to the current blend.",
  "mechanism": "The hypothesis is that provider repricing and changes in offer composition produce recurring sequences of published-median movements. Analog windows across series can capture these sequences, while equal weighting dilutes their signal with weaker forecasts in this slice.",
  "spec": {
    "when": {
      "all": [
        {"fact": "has_panel", "op": "==", "value": true},
        {"fact": "gate14", "op": "==", "value": false},
        {"fact": "in37", "op": "==", "value": false}
      ]
    },
    "do": {
      "action": "members_only",
      "members": ["analog"]
    }
  },
  "falsification": "Reject if pooled skill fails to rise overall or in either selection half, fewer than 200 cells across at least five series change, headline skill falls, or fewer than 90% of the 2000 ISO-week bootstrap resamples show improvement.",
  "prior_ids_used": [],
  "expects": "I expect pooled skill to improve, motivated by analog's higher skill at every horizon in the reported has_panel=true, gate14=false slice. Headline forecasts remain unchanged by construction. The report does not establish improvement in each half or bootstrap reliability. The in37 exclusion uses the explicitly permitted hindsight membership flag, so this proposal tests a restricted forecasting improvement rather than a fully origin-time selection policy."
}
